  AloneLines:
  - "Ash again. Sweep it out, it falls back in. Still, nobody else's footprints in it."
  - "The mountain grumbles, and I grumble back. That's conversation enough."
  - "{name}, you old fool, you could have lived somewhere green."
  - "No neighbours to borrow a broom from. No neighbours to steal one, either."
  - "Warm ground, quiet nights. The smoke keeps the visitors off. Mostly."
